erpret the Broad Money (M3) data?","answer":"$2b"},{"question":"What does the Broad Money (M3) data represent?","answer":"Broad Money (M3) data is a key indicator of the money supply, representing the total amount of money circulating within the economy, including cash, bank deposits, and other easily liquidable assets accessible for transactions and other economic activities.^Broad Money (M3) is a comprehensive measure that includes M1 (physical currency and demand deposits) and M2 (M1 plus savings deposits, small time deposits, and money market funds), plus time deposits, institutional money market funds, and other larger liquid assets."},{"question":"What is the significance of the Broad Money (M3) data?","answer":"Changes in the money supply, as indicated by M3, can have direct implications for inflation. An excessive increase in money supply can lead to inflationary pressures, while too little money supply growth can signal deflation.^M3 data is crucial for central banks to formulate monetary policies. It helps in decisions related to interest rates, liquidity management, and controlling inflation.^The level of broad money can reflect consumer confidence, spending habits, and savings trends within the economy.^M3 growth is often associated with increased availability of credit, which can stimulate economic growth through increased consumer spending and business investment.^A substantial part of India's economy still operates on cash transactions; hence, the money supply data can provide insights into economic liquidity and potential inflationary pressures."}],"related":[{"slug":"aggregate-bank-deposits","title":"Aggregate Bank Deposits"},{"slug":"bank-credit-industry","title":"Bank Credit - Industry"},{"slug":"bank-credit-personal-loans","title":"Bank Credit - Personal Loans"},{"slug":"bank-credit-services","title":"Bank Credit - Services"},{"slug":"cash-reserve-ratio-crr","title":"Cash Reserve Ratio (CRR)"},{"slug":"credit-deposit-ratio","title":"Credit-Deposit Ratio"},{"slug":"foreign-exchange-reserves","title":"Foreign Exchange Reserves"},{"slug":"foreign-portfolio-investments-fpis-debt","title":"Foreign Portfolio Investments (FPIs) - Debt"},{"slug":"marginal-cost-of-funds-based-lending-rates-mclr","title":"Marginal Cost of Funds based Lending Rates (MCLR)"},{"slug":"nifty-bank-pe-ratio","title":"NIFTY Bank P/E Ratio"},{"slug":"rbi-liquidity-net-laf","title":"RBI Liquidity (Net LAF)"},{"slug":"repo-rate","title":"Repo Rate"},{"slug":"statutory-liquidity-ratio-slr","title":"Statutory Liquidity Ratio (SLR)"},{"slug":"term-deposit-rate","title":"Term Deposit Rate"},{"slug":"weighted-average-lending-rate-on-fresh-rupee-loans-walr","title":"Weighted Average Lending Rate on Fresh Rupee Loans (WALR)"}],"title":"Money Supply (M3)","description":"India's M3 money supply stands at 19.10% for Sep 2026. Comparing this against nominal GDP shows how monetary expansion is tracking real economic activity.","headline":{"Absolute":"India's M3 money supply stands at ₹ 337,664.7 Billion for Sep 2026. Comparing this against nominal GDP shows how monetary expansion is tracking real economic activity.","Y-o-Y":"India's M3 money supply stands at 19.10% for Sep 2026. Comparing this against nominal GDP shows how monetary expansion is tracking real economic activity."},"source":"CMIE Economic Outlook, 1 Finance Research","source_url":"https://economicoutlook.cmie.com/","date_modified":"2026-09-01","scraped_at":"2026-10-17T15:41:11+00:00"}